framework ArchitectureDecisionRecord:
  requires problem and decision
  requires premise and evidence
  warns pending

domain ADR0027:
  description "ADR-0027 revision 1: Unified conscious agency and reaction-only psyche. Status Accepted. Supersedes ADR-0004; decision content D1-D8 is unchanged from the approved proposal."

problem P1:
  |
    ADR-0004 separates action selection and outward expression as independent
    consumers that cannot share raw inputs or outputs. That written constraint
    fragments the owner-requested conscious agency which coherently decides
    what the character does and says. Its origin as an authoring mistake is
    unverified; this record corrects the requirement mismatch without rewriting
    the historical rationale or pretending the old wording meant something else.

premise DRIVERS:
  |
    Keep non-deliberative affect dynamics distinct from conscious judgment and
    canonical adjudication. Protect observer-relative privacy and immutable
    battle contracts. Processing stages do not define separate conscious agents.

premise OPTIONS:
  |
    A: Retain independent action and expression judgments and add coordination;
    possible but introduces an unnecessary separation constraint for this goal.
    B: Use one conscious decision authority for goals, action and utterance,
    separate from psyche transitions and engine validation; proposed.
    C: Merge psyche, consciousness, world adjudication and narration into one
    unrestricted context; rejected because it mixes authority and visibility.

evidence E_OWNER:
  |
    The owner states that both action and speech belong to the character's
    conscious awareness; psyche should be an input-driven non-deliberative
    reaction model, with LLM use only in bounded special circumstances. The
    owner requests a superseding ADR, prechange impact and retained Seal history.
    This is authoring direction, not acceptance of the exact bytes of revision 1.

evidence E_SOURCE:
  |
    docs/adr/0004-versioned-lightweight-psyche-dynamics.md explicitly forbids
    mutual action/expression raw-context sharing in Stable component boundaries.
    docs/lightweight-psyche-adoptable-slice.md section 6 leaves migration of
    currentGoal, beliefs, free-text appraisal and ExpressionBrief undecided.

evidence E_BASELINE:
  |
    Prechange Seal adr/psyche-boundary is
    5a65ee9aeb1c0b082985e0e320521d014a7211ff0f4d8e50da4ebc8e10e56957.
    docs/evidence/sealgraph-psyche-baseline-2026-09-09.json records 16 initial
    sources, 15 downstream impact heads, no path truncation, source agreement,
    no initial stale and successful fsck. Coverage is not repository-wide.

decision D1 based_on P1, DRIVERS, OPTIONS, E_OWNER, E_SOURCE:
  |
    Propose one character conscious authority that derives an upper objective
    from authored personality, values and known relationship, assesses own
    abilities, resources, permitted engine knowledge and observed experience,
    and coherently decides short-term intent, action and utterance. Speech is
    an act of this consciousness, not a separate will. Shared conscious intent
    and task-relevant knowledge are permitted within its private boundary.
    Neither one LLM call nor a specific module topology is required.

decision D2 based_on D1, DRIVERS, E_SOURCE:
  |
    Psyche consumes validated normalized experience, bound psyche traits and
    prior private reaction state; it emits bounded affect/interpretation/impulse
    state and transition evidence. It does not reason over ability specifications,
    choose strategy, author speech or directly change world outcomes. Conscious
    judgment receives an explicit bounded projection of reaction state. Realized
    acts return via observer-safe experience. Separation is not total information
    isolation. Direct conscious regulation of psyche is not specified here.

decision D3 based_on D1, D2, DRIVERS:
  |
    The engine separately receives action and utterance proposals, validates
    legality, identity, visibility and applicable constraints, and commits actual
    results under existing rules. Separate receivers are not separate character
    minds. Desired speech effects do not directly change the counterpart's psyche
    or mechanics; recipient reaction and engine outcomes keep their owners.
    Public/narrator/opponent outputs exclude private goals and reasoning except
    what the character actually expresses and the observer may perceive.

decision D4 based_on D1, D2, D3, E_SOURCE, E_BASELINE:
  |
    Upon acceptance this ADR supersedes ADR-0004's governing decision, replacing
    the action-versus-expression independence and mutual-input/output ban with
    the boundary in D1-D3. Preserve ADR-0004's Initial explicit model, Learned
    target model, Psyche-only character embedding and Version and battle binding
    sections by reference to the exact prechange Seal in E_BASELINE, including
    normalization, excluded non-psyche material, bounded modulation, inspectable
    traits, shadow/calibration/privacy/replay acceptance and deterministic
    fallback. Action-facing and expression-facing tendencies may remain distinct
    data, but do not require distinct conscious owners. Research references remain
    non-adopted candidates. No model training or adoption is authorized here.

decision D5 based_on D2, D4, DRIVERS:
  |
    Preserve generation-specific routing: authoritative V1 normal-turn psyche
    remains no-call; missing features do not trigger LLM escalation. Existing
    prologue/aftermath and old-generation paths remain compatible. Special-moment
    LLM use is an extension to define by trigger, responsibility, inputs, maximum
    calls, cost, failure and revision binding before separate approval. This ADR
    neither invents a trigger nor claims existing phases fully implement that wish.

decision D6 based_on D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, E_SOURCE:
  |
    New implementation must specify unique writers/lifetimes for currentGoal,
    beliefs, appraisal and ExpressionBrief, conscious output schemas and explicit
    engine receivers. Initial migration covers CA-01/minimal CA-02 and dispositions
    for all seven PSYCHE-RESPONSIBILITY sites; full-path/old-battle compatibility
    may remain explicitly deferred rather than silently changed. ADR-0025/0026
    history, repetition, commit and bounded repair rules remain authoritative for
    their bound contracts; do not extend their repair closure by implication.
    Detailed new schemas, generations and call topology require the planned design
    and acceptance. This ADR does not itself authorize runtime changes or rollout.

decision D7 based_on D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D6:
  |
    Verify goal-dependent coherent action/speech, character and known-relationship
    differences, and lawful knowledge use. With identical psyche traits, prior
    state and normalized experience, changing ability metadata must not alter
    psyche transitions. Verify privacy, boundedness, generation/replay compatibility,
    no-call ceilings and engine ownership separately. Contract tests do not prove
    live-model behavioral improvement; paid evaluation is separately authorized.

decision D8 based_on D4, D6, E_BASELINE:
  |
    While Proposed, seal this candidate under a separate proposal REF linked to
    the prechange Seal, without advancing adr/psyche-boundary. After exact owner
    acceptance, preserve the old Seal, mark ADR-0004 Superseded with the successor
    link, continue the logical boundary REF with explicit reviewed revision
    assertions, and inspect stale/impact under recorded assertion scope. Review
    each affected document before relinking or resealing; stale is not automatic
    permission to edit Accepted decisions. Unregistered dependencies remain unknown.

evidence OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    On 2026-09-09, after the ADR-0004 versus ADR-0027 comparison, the owner said
    OKです。承認します。 The approved ADR-0027 revision 1 preacceptance SHA256 is
    74606d5bb31688b42c2ed228268e1f8d7976caac59fd328443f04949f054f055.
    The earlier request authorizes impact review, document correction and
    individual resealing. Runtime implementation and paid execution remain separate.

decision ACCEPTANCE based_on D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D6, D7, D8, OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    ADR-0027 revision 1 is Accepted and supersedes ADR-0004. D1-D8 retain their
    owner-approved wording; proposal/acceptance phase descriptions are historical
    conditions now resolved by this decision. Apply the documented responsibility
    correction and reviewed provenance succession. Detailed schemas, call topology,
    runtime migration and rollout remain subject to D5-D7 and the delivery plan.
